# LF-canonical prompt + workflow contract files (workflow authoring v2, d25d).
#
# The prompt front-matter canonical writer (rebar.llm.prompting.prompts.write_front_matter)
# emits LF, and prompt/workflow content hashes must be platform-stable — so a
# Windows checkout or core.autocrlf can never rewrite these to CRLF (which would
# defeat the \n-anchored front-matter fence and change the content hash). Pin the
# prompt files, the user prompt-override dir, the derived prompt index, and the
# workflow IR/index files to eol=lf.
src/rebar/llm/reviewers/*.md   eol=lf
.rebar/prompts/**              eol=lf
.rebar/prompts.index.json      eol=lf
.rebar/workflows/**            eol=lf

# The Windows sweep's deselect argument files (bug 6798-606d-37dc-46e7). A Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf would rewrite them to CRLF; pin LF so every platform holds the same bytes
# and tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py can compare lines exactly.
.github/windows-sweep-deselect/*.args eol=lf

# SHA-256-pinned vendored files (bug neglectful-acceptable-gerbil). Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would check these out CRLF and break their pins; -text keeps every
# checkout byte-identical to the committed blob.
.github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.json -text
tests/external/live_jira_dc/pycontribs-jira-LICENSE.txt -text
